    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Website RAG Customer Support Chatbot\n\nThis workflow contains two connected processes:\n\n## 1. Knowledge-base ingestion\nThe manual workflow maps a website with Firecrawl, removes unwanted and duplicate URLs, processes pages one at a time, extracts readable text, discards empty pages, splits useful content into overlapping chunks, creates Gemini embeddings, and stores the vectors in Pinecone.\n\n## 2. Customer-support chat\nThe chat trigger sends each message to a Gemini-powered AI agent. The agent searches the Pinecone knowledge base before answering questions about services, pricing, policies, FAQs, contact details, or other website content. Window memory preserves short conversational context.\n\n## Required setup\n- Replace `https://example.com/` with the website to index.\n- Connect Firecrawl, Pinecone, and Google Gemini credentials.\n- Replace `YOUR_PINECONE_INDEX` and `YOUR_PINECONE_NAMESPACE` everywhere.\n- Use the same Gemini embedding model for ingestion and retrieval.\n- Ensure the Pinecone index dimension matches the selected embedding model.\n\nRun the ingestion branch whenever the website content changes. Test the chat branch only after indexing completes successfully.",
        "height": 1104,
        "width": 592,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "cd4fca63-1379-4ccd-ad9b-eeea9f7d2e10",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2704,
        80
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Discover website pages\n\nFirecrawl maps the configured website and returns up to 100 page URLs. Replace `https://example.com/` with your own root domain and connect a Firecrawl credential before running the workflow.\n\nReview the returned URLs during your first test to confirm the crawl scope is appropriate.",
        "height": 608,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "43b535dd-391b-40c7-a163-a88f272864c8",
      "name": "Sticky Note - URL Discovery",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1440,
        -176
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Filter and process URLs safely\n\nThe code node removes duplicates, trailing slashes, XML files, and paths containing configured blocked keywords. The loop processes one URL at a time, while the delay node adds a two-second pause between requests.\n\nCustomize `blockedKeywords`, the Firecrawl result limit, and the delay for your website and crawl policy.",
        "height": 384,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "5d609d75-cf29-45a3-b80e-9be693677be5",
      "name": "Sticky Note - URL Filtering and Pacing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1120,
        48
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Fetch and clean page content\n\nEach URL is fetched with an HTTP Request node. The Set node keeps the page HTML and source URL, then the code node removes scripts, styles, tags, and excess whitespace to produce clean text for indexing.\n\nPages with fewer than 50 useful characters are skipped.",
        "height": 352,
        "width": 672,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "16c9cac5-f9de-493e-ba10-c33575899dc5",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Page Extraction",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -432,
        0
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
